// Lesson 8.3 — Player Attack: Fight Back
// The hitbox, the damage window, and the layer-mask reality.
// CORRECTED: Physics2D.queriesHitTriggers defaults to TRUE, so raycasts and
// overlaps DO return trigger colliders. A layer mask is the real tool, not
// the hope that triggers are invisible to queries.
//
// RUNG: 2 (guided build). The new mechanism here is a query about an AREA that
// comes back with a LIST — every query in the course before this one (the
// ground check in 6.2, the turret's range check in 3.1, the pickups in 2.1)
// asked about a point or a line and got one answer. So the shape of the file
// is given in full and exactly one line is left for the student: the overlap
// call itself. Everything around it is prior work — a trigger collider (2.1),
// a `LayerMask` (6.2, 7.2), the `Time.time` cooldown (3.3), a signed damage
// method (5.3) called on the boss's health (8.2).
//
// GROUND TRUTH (verified by reading AP_CS_P_Starter_Project, Unity 6000.6.0f1,
// and the earlier lessons — not by trusting this page's earlier draft):
//
//   ProjectSettings/Physics2DSettings.asset
//     m_QueriesHitTriggers: 1  — queries DO return trigger colliders, so the
//       whole first activity is load-bearing and correct. It is the Unity
//       default, not a local setting.
//     m_QueriesStartInColliders: 1 — a query that STARTS inside a collider can
//       report that collider, which is why the hitbox's own overlap of the
//       Player's CircleCollider2D is a real concern and the mask is not
//       optional.
//
//   Layers — CORRECTED. The draft of this page said "This project has no
//     custom physics layers yet". That is FALSE by Unit 8: 6.2 has the student
//     create `Ground`, and 7.2 says "You already created Ground back in 6.2"
//     and adds `Player`, `Enemy`, `Projectile` and `Decoration`. The cell now
//     says the buckets exist and the mask is what has to name them.
//
//   Docs — CORRECTED. The resources line described
//     ../docs/reference/unity-csharp-quickref.html as "the Physics2D query
//     family and layer masks". That page has NO Physics2D query rows and NO
//     layer-mask rows; its rows are vars, loops, input, transform, Time,
//     Instantiate/Destroy, collision callbacks, Animator, Mathf, List — plus
//     the `if (Time.time >= last + cooldown)` pattern and the sprite-mirror
//     line this script actually uses. The description now says that.
//
//   Player.prefab — root: Transform + PlayerController, tag `Player`, layer 0.
//     NO Rigidbody2D and NO Collider2D (both are the student's work in 2.1).
//     The only child is `Sprite` at local position (0, 0.6, -1), localScale 2
//     — which is why the hitbox must be parented to the ROOT and not to
//     `Sprite`, and why `flipX` (a render mirror) moves no collider.
//
//   The damage convention is `TakeDamage(int amount)` with a SIGNED amount:
//     positive hurts, negative heals (2.2 → moved onto StatManager in 5.3).
//     8.2 has the student write the same shape on the boss, so the walkthrough
//     passes a positive `attackDamage`. The boss health script's NAME is the
//     student's own, from 8.2 — the walkthrough says so rather than asserting
//     one.
//
